				<r3d:description language="eng">NASA&#039;s Physical Sciences Informatics (PSI) database functions as an open-access repository for data from a broad range of experimental platforms including the ISS, Space Shuttle, parabolic flights, Free Flyers, commercial cargo missions, and related ground-based studies. PSI focuses on research from six physical sciences disciplines:  Biophysics, Combustion Science, Complex Fluids/Soft Matter, Fluid Physics, Fundamental Physics and Materials Science.</r3d:description>
